# PLAN CLI BENCH — 12 agents for real ooda bench

File: openOODA/audit/plan_cli_bench.oot
Ship 3. Today cli/cmd_more.oo run_ooda_bench prints `ooda bench: ok`
and returns. That is a lie.

## 0. Done when

  1. `ooda bench FILE` typechecks FILE with the real compiler
     (same find_oodac + check path as `ooda check`).
  2. It prints wall time in ms from `now_ms` under `&TimeCap`.
     Example: `ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 12ms`
  3. Missing file: usage or ERR, exit 2. No `ok`.
  4. Check fail: non-zero exit. Still print that check failed.
     Do not print a fake time for a skipped run.
  5. Optional `--run`: after a passing check, run the file and
     print a second line with run ms.
  6. `ooda bench` with no file does not print `ooda bench: ok`.
  7. Help in cli/main.oo names the real command.
     Only this ship edits main.oo.

## 1. Waves

  Wave 0: COORD, RT, DOCS
  Wave 1: DE1, DE2, HARN
  Wave 2: HYG
  Wave 3: PV1, PV2, SEC, MEM
  Wave 4: INT
  Wave 5: COORD

## 2. Twelve agents

  COORD
    Worktree branch `wip/ooda-bench`.
    File lock: cmd_more.oo, main.oo, scripts/bench_smoke.oo.
    main.oo is 254 lines. Any help edit must stay <= 256.
    If help cannot fit, DE2 splits print_help into cli_help.oo
    and COORD records the split.

  DE1
    Own cli/cmd_more.oo.
    Replace the stub. Require a file path.
    t0 = now_ms(time); run check; t1 = now_ms(time).
    Print check ms. Exit with the check status.
    `--run` only after check pass.
    Do not print `ooda bench: ok`.

  DE2
    Own cli/main.oo.
    Add `&TimeCap` to main and pass it to run_ooda_bench.
    Update the help line: `ooda bench <file.oo> [--run]`.
    Do not change other command dispatch.
    If the signature change fails typecheck, stop and report.
    Do not invent a date +%s shell timer.

  RT
    Prove that a CLI main with `&FsCap, &SysCap, &TimeCap`
    already lowers. If it does not, that is a compiler/runtime
    blocker. Do not patch oodac or chs_rt. Write the error.
    Parent then either drops TimeCap (blocked) or waits.

  HARN
    scripts/bench_smoke.oo:
      bench fixtures/hello.oo prints a line matching
      `ooda bench: check ` and `ms`.
      Exit 0 on hello.
      bench with no args: not `ooda bench: ok`, exit != 0.
      bench missing.oo: exit != 0.
      Optional: --run hello prints a `run` ms line.

  PV1
    Attack: bench of a file that fails check. Must not print
    a successful run line. Must exit non-zero.

  PV2
    Attack: `ooda bench --run` with no file.
    Attack: path with `..` or an absolute path if write_file
    rules apply (bench is read + exec check only).
    Attack: the old stub string `ooda bench: ok` must be gone
    from the rebuilt binary (`strings`).

  SEC
    TimeCap only. No new SysCap shell timer.
    Do not exec the bench target with `sh -c`.
    Use the same check/run helpers as the product CLI.

  MEM
    Two now_ms calls per phase. No list growth.
    Hang budget 30 seconds on hello (emit+gcc if --run).

  INT
    Rebuild CLI with seed oodac after the TimeCap signature.
    Run bench_smoke twice.
    `ooda bench fixtures/hello.oo` twice; times may differ;
    both must be >= 0 and parse as an integer ms.
    Confirm oodac/oodac was not rebuilt.

  HYG
    cmd_more.oo is 96 lines. main.oo is 254.
    Split help if needed. No stub functions left that print ok
    for bench. Other stubs (em, migrate, install) stay. They
    are not this ship.

  DOCS
    No site edits. Audit note: bench measures check, not a
    microbench of user code, unless --run is passed.

## 3. Failure

  If TimeCap on CLI main does not typecheck with the seed
  compiler, COORD stops ship 3. Do not fall back to `date`.
  Ships 1 and 2 do not wait.
